{"id":"transfagarasan-transalpina","title":"Transfăgărășan and Transalpina","who":"Classic route · Romania's Carpathian high roads","when":"July to October, when the passes are open","vehicle":"Motorcycle, 4–5 days","kind":"moto","color":"#7c3aed","summary":"Two of Europe's great mountain roads in the Carpathians: the Transfăgărășan, carved by the army in the 1970s, with its wall of hairpins up to Bâlea Lake, and the Transalpina, higher and wilder, at 2,145 m. Between them, Dracula's real castle and the monasteries of Wallachia.","sources":[{"label":"Horizons Unlimited: Romania solo motorcycle trip (2025 thread)","url":"https://www.horizonsunlimited.com/hubb/europe/romania-solo-motorcycle-trip-sept-106165-print"},{"label":"Calimoto: motorcycle tours in Romania","url":"https://calimoto.com/en/blog/article/motorcycle-tours-romania"}],"approximate":"A common loop from Sibiu.","km":462,"bbox":[23.5541,45.0614,24.6778,45.9579],"stops":[{"name":"Sibiu","place":"Sibiu, Romania","at":[45.7974,24.1519],"text":"A Saxon old town with houses whose roof windows look like eyes.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Hermannstadt_Romania%2C_the_Small_Plaza.jpg/500px-Hermannstadt_Romania%2C_the_Small_Plaza.jpg","page":"Sibiu","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hermannstadt_Romania%2C_the_Small_Plaza.jpg","credit":"Zubi Travel","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Cârțișoara","place":"Cârțișoara, Romania","at":[45.7263,24.5745],"text":"The foot of the Transfăgărășan's north side.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/CartisoaraSB_%2811%29.JPG/500px-CartisoaraSB_%2811%29.JPG","page":"Cârțișoara","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CartisoaraSB_%2811%29.JPG","credit":"Țetcu Mircea Rareș","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Bâlea Lake","place":"Bâlea Lac","at":[45.6033,24.617],"text":"The famous ladder of hairpins to a glacial lake at 2,034 m, then a tunnel through the ridge.","source":{"label":"Calimoto: Romania","url":"https://calimoto.com/en/blog/article/motorcycle-tours-romania"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Romania-roads-DN7C.png/500px-Romania-roads-DN7C.png","page":"Transfăgărășan","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Romania-roads-DN7C.png","credit":"No machine-readable author provided. Qyd assumed (based on copyright claims).","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Poienari Castle","place":"Poienari Castle","at":[45.3539,24.6353],"text":"Past the Vidraru dam to the ruin of Vlad the Impaler's fortress, 1,480 steps up.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/PoienariCastle1.jpg/500px-PoienariCastle1.jpg","page":"Poenari Castle","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PoienariCastle1.jpg","credit":"Emmanuel BRUNNER Manu25","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Curtea de Argeș","place":"Curtea de Argeș, Romania","at":[45.1469,24.678],"text":"A carved white monastery church, resting place of Romania's kings.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Man_Curtea_de_Arges.SV.jpg/500px-Man_Curtea_de_Arges.SV.jpg","page":"Curtea de Argeș Cathedral","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Man_Curtea_de_Arges.SV.jpg","credit":"Alexandru Baboş Albabos","license":"CC BY 3.0"}},{"name":"Horezu","place":"Horezu, Romania","at":[45.1455,23.9938],"text":"A UNESCO monastery and potters' workshops.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Horezu_bis_man_SV.jpg/500px-Horezu_bis_man_SV.jpg","page":"Horezu Monastery","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horezu_bis_man_SV.jpg","credit":"Alexandru Baboș","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 ro"}},{"name":"Rânca","place":"Rânca, Romania","at":[45.2921,23.6889],"text":"Up from Novaci onto the Transalpina.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/RO_GJ_DN67C_Transalpina_7.jpg/500px-RO_GJ_DN67C_Transalpina_7.jpg","page":"Rânca","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RO_GJ_DN67C_Transalpina_7.jpg","credit":"Utilizator:Țetcu Mircea Rareș at ro.wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 2.5"}},{"name":"Transalpina","place":"Obârșia Lotrului","at":[45.4352,23.6302],"text":"Romania's highest road along the ridge at 2,145 m, sheep and shepherds' dogs on it.","source":{"label":"Horizons Unlimited thread (2025)","url":"https://www.horizonsunlimited.com/hubb/europe/romania-solo-motorcycle-trip-sept-106165-print"}},{"name":"Sebeș","place":"Sebeș, Romania","at":[45.9575,23.5692],"text":"Down the Sebeș valley past the Oașa lake.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Ansamblul_bisericii_evanghelice_din_Sebe%C8%99_4.jpg/500px-Ansamblul_bisericii_evanghelice_din_Sebe%C8%99_4.jpg","page":"Sebeș","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ansamblul_bisericii_evanghelice_din_Sebe%C8%99_4.jpg","credit":"Levente Nuber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Back in Sibiu","place":"Sibiu, Romania","at":[45.7974,24.1519],"text":"Back to the old town for the night.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Hermannstadt_Romania%2C_the_Small_Plaza.jpg/500px-Hermannstadt_Romania%2C_the_Small_Plaza.jpg","page":"Sibiu","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hermannstadt_Romania%2C_the_Small_Plaza.jpg","credit":"Zubi Travel","license":"Public domain"}}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":47,"line":[[45.7976,24.152],[45.7002,24.2486],[45.7589,24.448],[45.7627,24.5708],[45.7264,24.5747]]},{"by":"ride","km":30,"line":[[45.7264,24.5747],[45.6677,24.5772],[45.6776,24.5904],[45.637,24.6065],[45.6538,24.6095],[45.6043,24.6161]]},{"by":"ride","km":51,"line":[[45.6043,24.6161],[45.5923,24.6327],[45.5846,24.6225],[45.5848,24.6408],[45.5765,24.6144],[45.5441,24.5912],[45.4905,24.5833],[45.4759,24.6017],[45.4404,24.6069],[45.4337,24.5935],[45.4129,24.6197],[45.3747,24.6226],[45.3711,24.6109],[45.355,24.6358]]},{"by":"ride","km":26,"line":[[